# ChemLife Website Environment Variables Config Example
# Copy this file to .env.local and configure the values

# YouTube API Integration (For Podcasts playlist)
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=your-youtube-api-key-here
YOUTUBE_PLAYLIST_ID=UUw9YQ4V85x2n_L3mC0uE7yA # Default Channel Uploads playlist ID for ChemLife

# LinkedIn Company Feed Integration
LINKEDIN_ACCESS_TOKEN=your-linkedin-developer-token-here
LINKEDIN_ORGANIZATION_ID=your-linkedin-company-org-id-here

# Chatbot (Dr. Kukku and Dr. Mikku). Without both keys the chat pages show the bots as offline.
# On Hostinger, set these in hPanel's environment variables, then redeploy.
# Use an OpenAI key made for this website only, with a monthly budget limit set in the OpenAI dashboard.
OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key-here
PINECONE_API_KEY=your-pinecone-api-key-here
# Optional. The index must have been built with OpenAI text-embedding-3-small (1536 dimensions).
PINECONE_INDEX_NAME=chemlife-knowledge
# Optional. Most chat questions answered per day across the whole site (each costs about $0.001).
CHAT_DAILY_LIMIT=3000

# Google Analytics. Optional: the Measurement ID normally goes in src/lib/analytics.ts (GA_ID).
# This overrides it, e.g. to test with a separate GA4 property.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# Staging site only (any address other than chemlifeinnovations.com). Set it in the staging site's hPanel
# environment variables to make the site ask for a password. Any user name works.
# STAGING_PASSWORD=choose-a-password

# Contact form. Messages are emailed through Resend (resend.com); without a key the form says it's unavailable
# and offers the visitor a pre-filled email instead. The sender must be on a domain verified in Resend.
RESEND_API_KEY=your-resend-api-key-here
# Optional. Defaults: "ChemLife Website <website@notify.chemlifeinnovations.com>" and innovate@chemlifeinnovations.com.
# On the staging site, point CONTACT_TO at a tester's inbox so test messages don't reach the team.
# CONTACT_FROM=ChemLife Website <website@notify.chemlifeinnovations.com>
# CONTACT_TO=innovate@chemlifeinnovations.com

# Insights inbox (/admin/insights): the moderator chooses which posts from YouTube, the blog, Instagram and LinkedIn
# appear on the Insights page. Without DATABASE_URL and ADMIN_PASSWORD the page shows its built-in list.
# See src/lib/insights-store/README.md.
# The MySQL database (hPanel → Databases). URL-encode special characters in the password.
# DATABASE_URL=mysql://user:password@host:3306/database
# The moderator's password. Use a long one; changing it signs the moderator out.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=...
# Optional. Brings new Instagram posts in automatically: a long-lived token from a Meta app using the
# Instagram API with Instagram Login. The inbox renews it every week.
# INSTAGRAM_ACCESS_TOKEN=...
# Optional. Brings new LinkedIn company page posts in automatically: the address of a feed of the page's posts
# (RSS, Atom or JSON), e.g. from RSS.app's LinkedIn feed generator. Keep it private. New posts wait in the inbox.
# LINKEDIN_FEED_URL=https://rss.app/feeds/...
# Optional. Lets a scheduled job check for new posts: /api/admin/insights/sync?key=<this key>
# INSIGHTS_SYNC_KEY=...
# Staging only, for demos: "true" opens the inbox without signing in (ADMIN_PASSWORD isn't needed). It never
# applies on chemlifeinnovations.com. Remove it after the demo.
# INSIGHTS_DEMO=true
